The audit found no safe standalone implementations for the client-only hooks or generated-state methods. One live source-faithful gap remains in `FallingBlock`: vanilla centralizes the two-tick delay in `getDelayAfterPlace`, while Pumpkin duplicates the literal in both live scheduling hooks. I’ll wire a single helper into those callers and add a focused unit assertion; the remaining leads will be recorded as renamed, inlined, client-only, or data-modeled with grep evidence.
Finished the targeted audit; implementing the only live, source-faithful missing behavior structure and then documenting classifications.
