crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-3-//! This module handles the synchronization of inventory state between the server
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-4-//! and connected clients. It ensures that players see the correct items in slots,
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-5-//! cursor items, and container properties (like furnace progress).
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-6-//!
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-7-//! # Synchronization
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-8-//!
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-9-//! The sync handler manages:
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-10-//! - Full container content updates (sent when opening a container or on major changes)
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-11-//! - Individual slot updates (sent when a single slot changes)
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-12-//! - Cursor item updates (the item being held by the mouse cursor)
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs:13://! - Property updates (container-specific data like furnace burn time)
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-14-//!
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-15-//! # Revision Tracking
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-16-//!
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-17-//! Each synchronization message includes a revision number to ensure the client
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-18-//! and server stay in sync. If the client detects a desync, it can request a full
crates/pumpkin-inventory/src/sync_handler.rs-19-//! resynchronization.
