codex
One genuine gap is confirmed in `SmithingMenu`: the shared click handler’s pickup-all scan would include the result slot, while vanilla explicitly excludes it (`SmithingMenu.java:128-130`). The same class also lacks the live recipe-error property that vanilla updates when all three inputs are present but no result exists (`SmithingMenu.java:96-105,142-144`). I’m wiring both through the existing `on_slot_click` and screen-property synchronization paths; the other five classes have live Rust mappings or inline callers.
apply patch
