The spread-player audit found one additional real behavioral gap inside an otherwise mapped helper: Rust rejected liquids but allowed fire, whereas vanilla `Position.isSafe` rejects both (`SpreadPlayersCommand.java:364-368`). I’m adding that existing-tag check at the current `surface_y` call site; distance, grounding, clamping, and movement are already live inline equivalents.
