The six classes are largely false positives: the Rust side already has the live hooks or generated data models. I found one source-faithful behavioral defect worth shipping under the `FireBlock.canBurn` lead: `is_flammable` checks the burn-away odds, while vanilla `canBurn` checks ignite/spread odds (`FireBlock.java:269-287`). I’m correcting that live predicate and adding a focused pure test; the remaining leads will be recorded as renames, inlines, client-only, data-modeled, or blocked only with captured grep evidence.
